{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour `tests/interfaces` files contain audited prose that repeats behavior, narrates obvious setup, or states stale history. Scope was revalidated on `origin/main@0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only comments and true leading docstrings in the named blocks. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, constants, assertions, executable behavior, and exact tool directives.\n\nFor every changed Python file, parse pinned-before and final text with `type_comments=True`; remove only leading docstrings from modules, classes, functions, and async functions; normalize `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining ASTs to match. Compare shebang and directive-bearing physical lines separately and byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`, comments in `_rebar_repo_template` around the root commit, virgin-template invariant, post-context pin proof, and return — retain the no-preseed contract, why emptiness tests depend on it, and proof that the tracker is on `tickets`.\n- `tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py`, module prose and comments in the scoped copy/repair, virgin-template, identity, ref-isolation, and detached-upkeep tests — retain worktree/ref repointing, the proof that bare repair leaves the copy non-self-contained and damages its source, local identity reminting, and absence of detached maintenance.\n- `tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`, module and `_params` docstrings plus effect/store-invariance comments — retain one shared expectation across adapters and the future strict-xfail mechanism. Do not claim current known divergences: all `Case.xfail` maps are empty.\n- `tests/interfaces/write_parity_contract.py`, module, `Result`, `Case`, `_commit`, `_to_result`, and `execute` docstrings plus scoped table comments — retain row-field semantics, adapter-neutral setup, rejection identity, and store-invariance checks.\n\nPreserve `write_parity_contract._DESC`, all contract rows/runtime data, and `# noqa: BLE001` on the create-parity exception exactly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments, true leading docstrings, or adjacent blank lines in Scope; normalized AST equality and exact directive-line comparison both pass.\n- [ ] Each edited block is shorter and keeps its current non-obvious contract or rationale without moving repetition, history, or ornament elsewhere.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: path/block, immutable before citation, final-commit after citation (or DELETED plus neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, semantic-preservation verdict, bloat-removal verdict, and reviewer session.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing or failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] Focused tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard; `pytest tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py tests/interfaces/test_write_parity_oracle.py`; the session-log emptiness tests named by `tests/interfaces/conftest.py`; path-scoped `git diff --check`; and `make verify`. The independent TSV is authoritative for prose quality."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788615396097498001,"uuid":"fc55a127-ac29-40a7-95ae-c6cfd278d5cd"}